{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"## Root cause CONFIRMED on the live box — and the mechanism is broader than this ticket states\n\nReproduced on `i-00880b2c7f13527c5`, container `rebar-mcp-3118334705d2-8093`, with a two-arm discriminating experiment inside the running container:\n\n- **Arm A** — `git clone --single-branch --branch tickets $MCP_TICKETS_URL` into an **empty** dir → **rc=0**, 153,628 files. So the PAT (`PAT_LEN=40`), network, URL and branch are all healthy. Auth was never the problem.\n- **Arm B** — same clone into a **non-empty** dir → `fatal: destination path already exists and is not an empty directory.`\n\nLive store state before repair:\n\n```\nDIR=/var/gerrit/site/mcp-tickets\n.bridge_state  .ensure-applied  .env-id  .gitattributes\n.gitignore  .store-compat.json  .ticket-write.lock\ngit rev-parse HEAD  -> NO_HEAD\ngit remote -v       -> fatal: not a git repository\n```\n\n### The observed poisoning is NOT the one this ticket describes\n\nThis ticket's stated mechanism is \"a container removed mid-clone leaves orphaned objects and HEAD dangling at `refs/heads/.invalid`\". What is actually on the box is **no `.git` at all** — only `reviewbot-ensure-tickets.sh`'s marker files. Different path in, same trap. Both are caught by the `rev-parse --verify -q HEAD` gate in change 2244, so the fix is right; the *rationale* is incomplete and the test should cover this variant too.\n\nThe entry path is an ordering defect the current fix does not close:\n\n```sh\ngit clone ... || echo \"mcp: tickets store clone deferred (deploy canary)\" >&2\nfi\n# ensure runs UNCONDITIONALLY — including after the clone just failed\nsh /app/infra/scripts/reviewbot-ensure-tickets.sh \"${REBAR_TRACKER_DIR}\" || ...\n```\n\nOne failed clone → ensure runs anyway → ensure's marker files make the directory permanently non-empty → **every** subsequent clone fails arm-B style, forever. `|| echo` swallows git's real error, which is why \"clone deferred (deploy canary)\" was the only thing ever logged and the actual cause stayed invisible across every boot.\n\n### Consequence I got wrong earlier, corrected here\n\nI previously reported that the `store_uninitialized` read guard had fixed the false-empty reads in production. **It had not.** The guard tests `os.path.isdir(tracker)`, and the poisoned directory *exists* — it simply isn't a git repository. Verified live, before repair:\n\n```\nrebar.list_tickets() -> READ_OK count=0\n```\n\nA false empty, straight through the guard, on the deployed server. The guard closes \"directory absent\"; the actual production failure is \"directory present, not a store\". Filing that as its own defect — the predicate needs to require a usable store (resolvable HEAD), not merely an extant directory.\n\n### Repair applied (operator-authorized)\n\nBacked up the poisoned dir to `/var/tmp/mcp-tickets-poisoned-backup`, cleared it, re-cloned, re-ran ensure:\n\n```\nclone rc=0   HEAD=73ad5058bf   branch=tickets   remote=github.com/navapbc/rebar.git\ntickets visible: 2763   (was 0)\n```\n\nVerified end-to-end through the nginx-fronted endpoint (upstream `127.0.0.1:8093`, container healthy, `/health` → `{\"in_flight\":0}`) and by a real tracker read from an external MCP client, which now returns live ticket data.\n\nThis is a manual repair of one box; it does not make the trap unreachable. Durability still needs 2244 landed, plus the two gaps above."},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1787762962080120087,"uuid":"0357ed43-3a3e-49ae-adf6-cb990fe3e420"}